    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build is green. Here's a summary of what I changed to implement owner soft-delete.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` column mapped field (primitive `boolean`, defaults `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. A newly built owner is therefore `deleted = false`.\n\n**2. `DeleteOwner`** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`) \u2014 `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now flags the loaded owner `deleted = true` and `save`s it (retaining the row) instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`. The pipeline already responds 204 (2xx), and `GET` still loads by id, so the owner is returned afterward with `deleted` true.\n\n**3. Create-endpoint blocking checks** \u2014 both duplicate/identity checks now `continue` past any owner with `isDeleted()`:\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (exact identity-key 409)\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` (household duplicate 409)\n\nSo a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner was soft-deleted.\n\n**4. API contract** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema. The generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it automatically (name match), so `GET` serializes `$.deleted`.\n\n**5. DB schemas** \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The `DEFAULT FALSE` keeps the existing column-listed seed inserts valid.\n\n## Tests\nBoth new acceptance tests pass (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`), and the full `./mvnw test` suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** with no failures.\n\nOne note: I scoped the \"ignore deleted\" change to the two hard *blocking* checks (identity + household duplicate), per the spec's \"duplicate and identity checks \u2026 a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed.\" The soft-flagging step (`CheckPossibleDuplicate`) and the count steps still see all rows; let me know if you'd like deleted owners excluded there too.",
